\frac{7+10}{2}\cdot 3 = \frac{17}{2}\cdot 3 = \frac{51}{2}
\]square inches.  Thus the shaded region has area $(100)-\frac{51}{2} =\boxed{\frac{149}{2}}$. </think> <answer> \frac{149}{2} </answer>
